WEBVTT

NOTE
Kind: captions
Source: Articulate Closed Captions Editor
Source Version: 3.103.35301.0

00:00:00.009 --> 00:00:01.049
This is Beth.

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:05.190
Beth had another bad sleep last night and has woken up feeling tired.

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:08.500
Her curtains are shut and her room is dimly lit.

00:00:08.939 --> 00:00:09.449
Some days,

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:11.800
even small tasks feel impossible.

00:00:12.289 --> 00:00:14.199
Beth has a lot of tasks to do today,

00:00:14.289 --> 00:00:16.079
and she feels very overwhelmed.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:18.000
She doesn't know where to begin.

00:00:18.129 --> 00:00:21.520
The tasks have all blurred together into one huge task.

00:00:21.889 --> 00:00:24.450
Beth decides to write down the list of items,

00:00:24.649 --> 00:00:27.799
color coding them depending on how long they will take to complete.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:31.930
Breaking down the tasks by time makes them feel more manageable.

00:00:32.459 --> 00:00:34.970
Beth starts off with the shorter tasks first,

00:00:35.459 --> 00:00:38.819
watering her plants and then sending a couple of emails.

00:00:38.979 --> 00:00:40.540
Starting with short tasks,

00:00:40.619 --> 00:00:43.380
first helps to build momentum and encourages Beth

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:45.729
to continue working through her to do list.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.709
Beth makes sure to tidy her room before then

00:00:48.709 --> 00:00:51.409
creating the poster design for her work project.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:52.799
Once this is done,

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:55.020
she can start working on her assignment.

00:00:55.619 --> 00:00:57.299
Beth has reached the end of the day.

00:00:57.759 --> 00:00:59.599
She still has her assignment to finish,

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:02.880
but the important thing is that progress has been made today.

00:01:03.409 --> 00:01:04.529
Beth feels lighter,

00:01:04.769 --> 00:01:09.400
proud of herself for making a start and working her way through most of her tasks.

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:12.129
By breaking tasks down and starting small,

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:16.889
Beth now has much less to do the next day and can go to bed feeling less overwhelmed.

